  "analysis": "Disk shows 0 available on a 984G fuse-overlayfs (960G used). apt lists use 49M. The install failed needing 70MB for archives. I should clean apt caches and find what's consuming space. The patch history mentions a prior task that may have left large files, but /app is empty now. Let me clean and inspect larger space consumers.",
  "plan": "1. Run apt-get clean to free the lists (49M). 2. Check df again. 3. Find large directories consuming space (e.g., /usr, /var) to free more if needed. 4. Retry install.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "apt-get clean 2>&1; df -h / 2>&1\n",
      "duration": 1.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "du -sh /usr /var /opt /root /home 2>/dev/null\n",
      "duration": 2.0
    }
  ]
}

