  "plan": "1. Mount a 4G tmpfs over /var/cache/apt/archives so apt's free-space check passes with genuine space. 2. Retry installing gcc, make, wget. 3. Verify gcc/gcov/make/wget are available.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "mount -t tmpfs -o size=4g tmpfs /var/cache/apt/archives 2>&1; df -h /var/cache/apt/archives\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "apt-get -o Acquire::Check-Free-Space=false install -y gcc make wget 2>&1 | tail -10\n",
      "duration": 60.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The mount was denied (no CAP_SYS_ADMIN in this container), and `-o Acquire::Check-Free-Space=false` did not suppress apt's free-space pre-check even though real writes succeed (dd wrote 50MB fine). The fuse-overlayfs reports 0 avail via statvfs but actual writes work. I need another way to either bypass the check or give the apt cache a filesystem that reports honest free space. I'll probe whether `unshare -m` gives me a mount namespace where I can mount tmpfs over the apt cache, and what download tools (python3/perl) are available as a fallback.",
  "plan": "1. Probe `unshare -m` availability and presence of python3/perl/curl. 2. If unshare works, mount a tmpfs over /var/cache/apt/archives inside the namespace and run apt-get to install gcc/make/wget — the tmpfs will report real free space so the check passes. 3. If unshare fails, fall back to fetching .debs with python3. I will NOT run any of the AVOID-list commands.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "unshare -m true 2>&1; echo UNSHARE_EXIT=$?\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "which python3 perl curl 2>&1; echo '---'\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "Mounting tmpfs is denied (no CAP_SYS_ADMIN) and unshare fails. python3 and perl are available; no curl but wget is itself a target to install. Real writes work (dd succeeded), but apt's statvfs free-space pre-check on /var/cache/apt/archives aborts the install and `-o Acquire::Check-Free-Space=false` didn't suppress it. The reliable bypass: use `apt-get --print-uris` to list the .deb URLs, download them with python3 (which doesn't do a free-space check), then install with dpkg. I will NOT run any of the AVOID-list commands.",
  "plan": "1. Generate the list of .deb URLs with `apt-get --print-uris`. 2. Inspect to confirm it captured the packages. 3. In the next batch, download them with python3 into /tmp/debs and install via dpkg -i. This fully avoids apt's free-space check.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "apt-get -o Acquire::Check-Free-Space=false --print-uris install gcc make wget > /tmp/uris.txt 2>/dev/null; wc -l /tmp/uris.txt; head -5 /tmp/uris.txt\n",
      "duration": 2.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The `apt-get --print-uris` wrote to /tmp/uris.txt but the output appears empty (head showed nothing). The print-uris likely needs the package download list resolved; possibly apt requires `apt-get update` done and the uris formatting. Let me inspect the file to see what was captured.",
  "plan": "1. Inspect /tmp/uris.txt content and size. 2. If empty, re-run print-uris without redirecting stderr to see errors. 3. Once I have the .deb URLs, download them with python3 and install via dpkg.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat /tmp/uris.txt | head -20; echo '---LINES---'; wc -l /tmp/uris.txt\n",
      "duration": 0.3
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The --print-uris output contains 120 lines mixing apt's informational messages with the actual URI lines. The real URI lines are the ones starting with a single quote (format: 'URL' filename size sha256:...). I'll filter those, download each .deb with python3 (which bypasses apt's free-space statvfs check), then install via dpkg. Real disk writes work, so this will succeed. I will NOT run any AVOID-list commands.",
  "plan": "1. Re-run apt-get --print-uris and extract only lines beginning with a quote into a clean list. 2. Write a python3 script to download each .deb into /tmp/debs. 3. Install them with dpkg -i. 4. Verify gcc/gcov/make/wget. Then proceed to SQLite.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "apt-get -o Acquire::Check-Free-Space=false --print-uris install gcc make wget 2>/dev/null | grep \"^'\" > /tmp/urls.txt; wc -l /tmp/urls.txt; head -3 /tmp/urls.txt\n",
      "duration": 2.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The command to extract URI lines is running. I need to see its output (number of URLs and sample) before proceeding to download.",
  "plan": "Wait for the output of the grep command to confirm URL extraction worked, then download the .debs with python3.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "",
      "duration": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

